Let's find the distance Fen crossed in each section of the race. Then we can add all these up to find the total distance.

For example, she rode a bicycle for $x$ hours at an average speed of $20$ kilometers per hour, so Fen crossed $20x$ kilometers in the cycling section of the race:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(20\,\dfrac{\text{kilometers}}{\text{hour}}\right)\left(x\,\text{hours}\right)
\\\\
&=20x\,\dfrac{\text{kilometers}}{\cancel{\text{hour}}}\cdot\,\cancel{\text{hours}}
\\\\
&=20x\,\text{kilometers}
\end{align}$
